# quiet-uart under qemu-system-mips -- 2026-08-29, RUNSHEET P3

# THE CONTROL: no marks in the image, nothing on the wire

host        Linux 6.6.87.2-microsoft-standard-WSL2
qemu        QEMU emulator version 8.2.2 (Debian 1:8.2.2+ds-0ubuntu1.18)
tool        tools/deskchan.py 1.0   (NOT tools/rlxprobe/qemu-run.sh --
            different entry mechanism, different CPU, different UART;
            qemu/README.md says which is which and why it matters)
machine     -M malta -m 128 -cpu 4Kc -bios <4-instruction stub>
            -device loader,file=<image>,addr=0,force-raw=on
            -serial null -serial null -serial file:   (index 2 = CBUS)
seconds     30 (nothing here halts; the run is bounded by timeout)

## the DEVICE artefact this run is about
    vmlinux    3968113 bytes  sha256 ded501a356986274d3526fa1363895ed1e0622d41c3bf2bca88a05efb7d59b8a
    nfjrom     1027072 bytes  sha256 09f5eea5ae1f7f5b684fbfabb79dfd6a66348f7787c82e4739c6af1a7d983007   <- what gets uploaded
    entry      0x80003600   (kernelStartAddr, read out of the nfjrom header)

## the qemu image -- NOT the same bytes
    decompressed image 3472384 bytes  sha256 d7e705fc0c749d3944a31b73b7c89a0fe795e2e75e3a4b0c01a203f03f55b319
    Two declared patches, and nothing else:
      COP3 -> nop   4 word(s) -> nop: 0x8000233C(4c880000) 0x8000234C(4c880800) 0x80002398(4c882000) 0x800023A8(4c882800)
                    qemu 4Kc raises Coprocessor Unusable on these; the
                    channel therefore SKIPS the Lexra IMEM/DMEM setup
      UART          prom_putchar 0x8000B080+100 -> 5 word(s): 3c02b800 x2 34462014 x1 34452008 x1 34422000 x1
                    0xB8002000/08/14 -> 0xBF000900/10/28, malta CBUS.
                    Five words inside prom_putchar, window from the
                    symbol table. On the device none of this is present.

## the run
    distinct PCs translated  942   (of them KSEG0: 938)
    translated blocks        168
    last block               0x80006B94  bsp_machine_halt+0
    KSEG0 reach              0x800022D0 .. 0x802B8E14

## the capture
    quiet-uart.txt   0 bytes
    sha256       e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855
    EMPTY ON PURPOSE. This is C5: an image with no marks in it must
    print nothing through the same channel. A zero-byte file is the
    measurement, and without it the other two captures would be
    evidence that a UART works rather than that a mark ran.

